```

The inner loop increments both `r_idx` and `i`. If `u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0 > u4_num_st_curr_before + u4_num_st_curr_after + u4_num_lt_curr`, then the while loop would continue but the inner for loops would not execute because `i` would already be at the max. Wait, no - the inner for loops re-initialize `i = 0` each time. So the while loop would keep cycling through the same entries.

Actually wait, let me re-read the code more carefully:

